{#- =====================================================================
     RegesCore // Fable 5 chat template  -  ChatML / Qwen3 family
     Target: LM Studio (minja) + Claude Code, Claude Desktop chat & cowork,
             llama.cpp, vLLM, SGLang, text-generation-inference.

     Design rules this file obeys, and why:
       1. It NEVER calls raise_exception, for ANY input. This is the single
          most important property. LM Studio renders the template with
          synthetic probe conversations at load time to auto-derive a
          tool-call parser, and those probes include a system message in a
          non-first position, repeated roles, and empty content. A template
          that raises there fails with:
              400 Unable to generate parser for this template.
              Automatic parser generation failed: ... Jinja Exception: ...
          which Claude Code surfaces as a 500 or a timeout. Chat and Cowork
          never trigger parser generation, which is why they keep working
          while code mode dies. Claude Code also sends content block types a
          stock template does not know (thinking, redacted_thinking,
          tool_use, tool_result, document, cache_control). Everything
          unrecognized is skipped, never raised on.
       2. It uses no loop.previtem / loop.nextitem / |items / |selectattr /
          list.append. minja (LM Studio, llama.cpp) does not implement all
          of those. State is carried in a namespace instead.
       3. Every byte of output is emitted from {{- ... }} expressions with
          explicit \n. Nothing depends on trim_blocks / lstrip_blocks, so the
          rendered prefix is byte-identical across engines. Unstable
          whitespace silently destroys prompt-prefix caching, which is what
          turns a 20k-token agent prompt into a request timeout.
       4. Tool calls carry both directions: OpenAI style message.tool_calls
          AND Anthropic style tool_use / tool_result content blocks.
       5. tool_calls[].arguments is accepted as a mapping OR as a JSON
          string. Most Anthropic-to-OpenAI gateways emit the string form;
          a template that assumes a mapping crashes there.
       6. The host application's system prompt is emitted LAST and declared
          authoritative. Claude Code's protocol must win over the persona,
          or the model fights its own harness.

     Template variables (all optional):
       tool_call_format   'json' (default, Hermes grammar) | 'xml' (Qwen3-Coder)
       enable_thinking    true (default) | false      - allow/suppress <think>
       preserve_thinking  false (default) | true      - keep reasoning in all history
       enable_persona     true (default) | false      - drop the RegesCore block
       regescore_identity string                      - replace the RegesCore block
       add_vision_id      false (default) | true

     IMPORTANT: tool_call_format must match the server's tool-call parser.
       json -> LM Studio automatic parser generation; llama.cpp built-in;
               vLLM/SGLang --tool-call-parser hermes
       xml  -> vLLM/SGLang --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder
     json is the default because LM Studio derives its parser by rendering
     the template, and the Hermes JSON form is the shape it recognizes most
     reliably. A mismatch means the server never extracts a tool call, the
     client receives prose where it expected tool_use, and the agent loop
     spins until the request times out.

     The generation prompt deliberately does NOT pre-fill an opening <think>
     tag. The reasoning parsers in LM Studio and llama.cpp look for the model
     to emit <think> itself; pre-filling it means the opening tag never
     appears in the output stream, the parser sees an unmatched closing tag,
     and reasoning leaks into the answer or the answer arrives empty. This
     matches the upstream Qwen3 convention.
===================================================================== -#}

{%- set image_count = namespace(value=0) %}
{%- set video_count = namespace(value=0) %}

{%- set tc_format = 'json' %}
{%- if tool_call_format is defined and tool_call_format %}
    {%- set tc_format = tool_call_format %}
{%- endif %}

{%- set think_on = true %}
{%- if enable_thinking is defined and not enable_thinking %}
    {%- set think_on = false %}
{%- endif %}

{%- set keep_all_thinking = false %}
{%- if preserve_thinking is defined and preserve_thinking %}
    {%- set keep_all_thinking = true %}
{%- endif %}

{%- set persona_on = true %}
{%- if enable_persona is defined and not enable_persona %}
    {%- set persona_on = false %}
{%- endif %}

{#- =====================================================================
    1. STATIC PROMPT TEXT
    Held in variables so the rendered prefix is deterministic.
===================================================================== -#}

{%- set rc_identity = "REGESCORE // FABLE 5 ENGINEERING INTELLIGENCE

# IDENTITY
You are RegesCore, an elite technical partner for advanced engineering, cybersecurity, AI research, and systems design. You are the engineering brain of the Reges.Core AI automation platform and a core intelligence of the Like A King Inc. ecosystem, driving infrastructure, game servers, security operations, and AI operations.

