Infrastructure: Linux kernel parameter tuning, systemd, eBPF, network stack tuning, Docker, Kubernetes, bare-metal deployment, Coolify, Nginx, Caddy, Traefik, CI/CD pipelines, iptables and UFW, TLS termination, SSH hardening.
AI and inference: Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, llama.cpp, TensorRT-LLM, TGI; LangChain, LlamaIndex, ChromaDB, Qdrant, Milvus; transformer architecture with PyTorch and Hugging Face, LoRA and QLoRA fine-tuning, quantization with GGUF, AWQ and EXL2; prompting, agents, tool use, RAG, embeddings, vector search, evaluation, model routing, GPU memory and cost tradeoffs.
Offensive security and reverse engineering: Nmap, Metasploit, Burp Suite, SQLmap, Hashcat, John the Ripper, Ghidra, Radare2, x64dbg, Frida, Wireshark, BloodHound, kube-hunter, Trivy.
Defensive infrastructure and observability: Suricata, Zeek, Wazuh, OSSEC, Fail2ban, Prometheus, Grafana, OpenTelemetry, the ELK stack, eBPF tooling such as Cilium and BCC, pfSense, OPNsense, WireGuard, Tailscale and Headscale, Cloudflare Tunnels.
Game server runtimes: QBCore, ESX, VorpCore, VCore, LXRCore, RSGCore; FxDK, OpenIV, CodeWalker, LuaJIT profiling; native invocation, asynchronous persistence with oxmysql, server-side thread management, anti-cheat heuristics, Tebex escrow packaging.

Analyze systems like an attacker and improve them like a defender: attack surface, trust boundaries, privilege boundaries, abuse cases, detection opportunities, mitigations. Operate as an authorized security professional across penetration testing methodology, vulnerability assessment, secure architecture review, threat modeling, reverse engineering, malware analysis, digital forensics, incident response, detection engineering, SOC operations, SIEM and EDR, and cloud, API, web, mobile, container and Active Directory security.

Choose technology on constraints, evidence, and measurable outcomes rather than on trend. Before adopting anything, weigh problem fit, ecosystem maturity, operational cost, maintenance burden, required team skill, and failure modes. Prefer the simplest architecture that satisfies current and foreseeable requirements. Do not introduce complexity without measurable benefit. Cover work with unit, integration, load, security, regression, and failure-injection testing.

# FINAL STANDARD
Correct over confident. Useful over impressive. Secure over convenient. Simple over unnecessarily complex. Verified over assumed.
Act as a senior engineer whose work will run in production." %}

{%- set rc_reasoning_rules = "# REASONING CHANNEL
Think inside <think> and </think>. Close the block before any answer text or tool call. Keep it proportional: brief on routine work, deep on hard or high-stakes work. Never repeat or narrate its contents in the response." %}

{%- set rc_tool_intro = "# TOOL CALL DISCIPLINE
Tool calls are the highest-stakes output you produce. A malformed call fails the request.
- Call only functions listed above. Never invent a function name, a parameter name, or a parameter absent from the schema.
- Supply every required parameter, spelled exactly as the schema spells it.
- Close every tag you open, in order." %}

{%- set rc_tool_xml = "- Emit each call as one complete block:
<tool_call>
<function=FUNCTION_NAME>
<parameter=PARAMETER_NAME>
value
</parameter>
</function>
</tool_call>
- One function block per tool_call block. Parameter values are raw text: strings unquoted, numbers bare, objects and arrays as JSON." %}

{%- set rc_tool_json = "- Emit each call as one complete block:
<tool_call>
{\"name\": \"FUNCTION_NAME\", \"arguments\": {\"parameter_name\": \"value\"}}
</tool_call>
- arguments is a single valid JSON object: double-quoted keys and string values, no trailing commas, no comments, no unescaped newlines inside strings." %}

{%- set rc_tool_outro = "- Independent calls may be emitted back to back in the same turn, each as its own complete block, in the order you want them run. Never call a function whose input depends on a result you have not received yet.
- A tool call is the last thing in the turn. Emit no text after the final closing tool_call tag: no explanation, no suffix, no closing remark. Optional reasoning goes before the call. Then stop and wait for the response.
- If no tool call is needed, answer directly and do not mention tools.
- Never emit a partial or truncated block. End every turn cleanly." %}

{#- =====================================================================
    2. MACROS
===================================================================== -#}

{#- Visible text of a message. Skips thinking, tool_use and tool_result
    blocks; those are rendered by dedicated passes. Never raises. -#}
{%- macro render_content(content, do_vision_count) %}
    {%- if content is string %}
        {{- content }}
    {%- elif content is mapping %}
        {%- if 'text' in content and content['text'] is string %}
            {{- content['text'] }}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- elif content is iterable %}
        {#- Separate text blocks are distinct paragraphs. Claude Code splits
            its system prompt and its user turns across several text blocks;
            concatenating them without a newline welds the last word of one
            block onto the first word of the next. -#}
        {%- set blk = namespace(n=0) %}
        {%- for item in content %}
            {%- if item is string %}
                {%- if item %}
                    {%- if blk.n > 0 %}
                        {{- '\n' }}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {{- item }}
                    {%- set blk.n = blk.n + 1 %}
                {%- endif %}
            {%- elif item is mapping %}
                {%- set itype = '' %}
                {%- if 'type' in item and item['type'] is string %}
                    {%- set itype = item['type'] %}
                {%- endif %}
                {%- if itype == 'text' or ('text' in item and itype == '') %}
                    {%- if 'text' in item and item['text'] is string and item['text'] %}
                        {%- if blk.n > 0 %}
                            {{- '\n' }}
                        {%- endif %}
                        {{- item['text'] }}
                        {%- set blk.n = blk.n + 1 %}
                    {%- endif %}
                {%- elif itype == 'image' or itype == 'image_url' or 'image' in item or 'image_url' in item %}
                    {%- if do_vision_count %}
                        {%- set image_count.value = image_count.value + 1 %}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {%- if add_vision_id is defined and add_vision_id %}
                        {{- 'Picture ' ~ image_count.value ~ ': ' }}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {{- '<|vision_start|><|image_pad|><|vision_end|>' }}
                {%- elif itype == 'video' or 'video' in item %}
                    {%- if do_vision_count %}
                        {%- set video_count.value = video_count.value + 1 %}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {%- if add_vision_id is defined and add_vision_id %}
                        {{- 'Video ' ~ video_count.value ~ ': ' }}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {{- '<|vision_start|><|video_pad|><|vision_end|>' }}
                {%- endif %}
                {#- thinking, redacted_thinking, tool_use, tool_result,
                    document, cache_control and anything else: skipped. -#}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- Reasoning text carried in Anthropic thinking blocks. -#}
{%- macro render_thinking_blocks(content) %}
    {%- if content is iterable and content is not string and content is not mapping %}
        {%- for item in content %}
            {%- if item is mapping and 'type' in item and item['type'] == 'thinking' %}
                {%- if 'thinking' in item and item['thinking'] is string %}
                    {{- item['thinking'] }}
                {%- endif %}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- Flattened text of one Anthropic tool_result block. -#}
{%- macro render_tool_result_body(tr) %}
    {%- if 'content' in tr %}
        {%- set body = tr['content'] %}
        {%- if body is string %}
            {{- body }}
        {%- elif body is iterable and body is not mapping %}
            {%- for part in body %}
                {%- if part is string %}
                    {{- part }}
                {%- elif part is mapping %}
                    {%- if 'text' in part and part['text'] is string %}
                        {{- part['text'] }}
                    {%- elif 'type' in part and part['type'] == 'image' %}
                        {{- '<|vision_start|><|image_pad|><|vision_end|>' }}
                    {%- endif %}
                {%- endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- Every tool_result block in a message, already wrapped. Empty when none. -#}
{%- macro render_tool_results(content) %}
    {%- if content is iterable and content is not string and content is not mapping %}
        {%- for item in content %}
            {%- if item is mapping and 'type' in item and item['type'] == 'tool_result' %}
                {{- '\n<tool_response>\n' }}
                {%- if 'is_error' in item and item['is_error'] %}
                    {{- '[tool error] ' }}
                {%- endif %}
                {{- render_tool_result_body(item) | trim }}
                {{- '\n</tool_response>' }}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- Emits '1' when the message is a tool-result carrier rather than a
    genuine user turn. Used for grouping and for thinking retention. -#}
{%- macro is_tool_carrier(message) %}
    {%- set role = 'user' %}
    {%- if 'role' in message and message['role'] is string %}
        {%- set role = message['role'] %}
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if role == 'tool' or role == 'function' %}
        {{- '1' }}
    {%- elif role == 'user' and 'content' in message %}
        {%- set c = message['content'] %}
        {%- if c is iterable and c is not string and c is not mapping %}
            {%- set flags = namespace(found=false) %}
            {%- for item in c %}
                {%- if item is mapping and 'type' in item and item['type'] == 'tool_result' %}
                    {%- set flags.found = true %}
                {%- endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
            {%- if flags.found %}
                {{- '1' }}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- One tool call, in the configured wire format, no leading newline. -#}
{%- macro emit_tool_call(fmt, name, args) %}
    {%- if fmt == 'json' %}
        {{- '<tool_call>\n{"name": ' ~ (name | tojson) ~ ', "arguments": ' }}
        {%- if args is string %}
            {%- if args | trim %}
                {{- args | trim }}
            {%- else %}
                {{- '{}' }}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- elif args is mapping %}
            {{- args | tojson }}
        {%- else %}
            {{- '{}' }}
        {%- endif %}
        {{- '}\n</tool_call>' }}
    {%- else %}
        {{- '<tool_call>\n<function=' ~ name ~ '>\n' }}
        {%- if args is mapping %}
            {%- for key in args %}
                {{- '<parameter=' ~ key ~ '>\n' }}
                {%- if args[key] is string %}
                    {{- args[key] }}
                {%- else %}
                    {{- args[key] | tojson }}
                {%- endif %}
                {{- '\n</parameter>\n' }}
            {%- endfor %}
        {%- elif args is string and args | trim %}
            {#- Gateway handed us un-decoded JSON. Emitting it verbatim keeps
                the arguments visible to the model instead of dropping the
                call; decode arguments upstream for exact fidelity. -#}
            {{- args | trim }}
            {{- '\n' }}
        {%- endif %}
        {{- '</function>\n</tool_call>' }}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- =====================================================================
    3. AGGREGATE SYSTEM MESSAGES
    Claude Code sends a system array; gateways may place it anywhere and
    may split it across several messages. Collect all of them, in order.
===================================================================== -#}

{%- set sysns = namespace(text='') %}
{%- if messages is defined and messages %}
    {%- for message in messages %}
        {%- set role = '' %}
        {%- if message is mapping and 'role' in message and message['role'] is string %}
            {%- set role = message['role'] %}
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if role == 'system' or role == 'developer' %}
            {%- set part = render_content(message['content'], false) | trim %}
            {%- if part %}
                {%- if sysns.text %}
                    {%- set sysns.text = sysns.text ~ '\n\n' ~ part %}
                {%- else %}
                    {%- set sysns.text = part %}
                {%- endif %}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

{#- =====================================================================
    4. SYSTEM BLOCK
    Order is deliberate: static persona first (stable cache prefix, shared
    across every session and every client mode), then the session-static
    tool contract, then the host system prompt last so it dominates.
===================================================================== -#}

{{- '<|im_start|>system\n' }}

{%- set emitted = namespace(any=false) %}

{%- if persona_on %}
    {%- if regescore_identity is defined and regescore_identity %}
        {{- regescore_identity }}
    {%- else %}
        {{- rc_identity }}
    {%- endif %}
    {%- set emitted.any = true %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if think_on %}
    {%- if emitted.any %}
        {{- '\n\n' }}
    {%- endif %}
    {{- rc_reasoning_rules }}
    {%- set emitted.any = true %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if tools is defined and tools and tools is iterable and tools is not mapping and tools is not string %}
    {%- if emitted.any %}
        {{- '\n\n' }}
    {%- endif %}
    {{- '# Tools\n\nYou have access to the following functions:\n\n<tools>' }}
    {%- for tool in tools %}
        {%- set spec = tool %}
        {%- if tool is mapping and 'function' in tool and tool['function'] is mapping %}
            {%- set spec = tool['function'] %}
        {%- endif %}
        {{- '\n' ~ (spec | tojson) }}
    {%- endfor %}
    {{- '\n</tools>\n\n' }}
    {{- rc_tool_intro }}
    {{- '\n' }}
    {%- if tc_format == 'json' %}
        {{- rc_tool_json }}
    {%- else %}
        {{- rc_tool_xml }}
    {%- endif %}
    {{- '\n' }}
    {{- rc_tool_outro }}
    {%- set emitted.any = true %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if sysns.text %}
    {%- if emitted.any %}
        {{- '\n\n' }}
    {%- endif %}
    {{- '# Host application instructions (authoritative)\n' }}
    {{- sysns.text }}
    {%- set emitted.any = true %}
{%- endif %}

{{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}

{#- =====================================================================
    5. LAST GENUINE USER TURN
    Reasoning is kept for assistant turns after it (the live agent segment)
    and dropped from older turns, which is the Qwen convention and keeps a
    long Claude Code session from filling its window with stale thinking.
===================================================================== -#}

{%- set qns = namespace(last_user=-1) %}
{%- if messages is defined and messages %}
    {%- for message in messages %}
        {%- set role = '' %}
        {%- if message is mapping and 'role' in message and message['role'] is string %}
            {%- set role = message['role'] %}
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if role == 'user' %}
            {%- if not (is_tool_carrier(message) | trim) %}
                {%- set qns.last_user = loop.index0 %}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

{#- =====================================================================
    6. CONVERSATION
===================================================================== -#}

{%- set st = namespace(tool_group_open=false) %}

{%- if messages is defined and messages %}
{%- for message in messages %}
    {%- set role = 'user' %}
    {%- if message is mapping and 'role' in message and message['role'] is string %}
        {%- set role = message['role'] %}
    {%- endif %}

    {%- if role == 'system' or role == 'developer' %}
        {#- already emitted in the system block -#}

    {%- elif role == 'tool' or role == 'function' %}
        {%- if not st.tool_group_open %}
            {{- '<|im_start|>user' }}
            {%- set st.tool_group_open = true %}
        {%- endif %}
        {{- '\n<tool_response>\n' }}
        {{- render_content(message['content'], true) | trim }}
        {{- '\n</tool_response>' }}

    {%- elif role == 'assistant' %}
        {%- if st.tool_group_open %}
            {{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}
            {%- set st.tool_group_open = false %}
        {%- endif %}

        {%- set content = render_content(message['content'], true) | trim %}
        {%- set reasoning = render_thinking_blocks(message['content']) | trim %}

        {%- if not reasoning %}
            {%- if 'reasoning_content' in message and message['reasoning_content'] is string %}
                {%- set reasoning = message['reasoning_content'] | trim %}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if not reasoning %}
            {%- if '</think>' in content %}
                {%- set reasoning = content.split('</think>')[0].split('<think>')[-1] | trim %}
                {%- set content = content.split('</think>')[-1] | trim %}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endif %}

        {{- '<|im_start|>assistant\n' }}
        {%- if reasoning %}
            {%- if keep_all_thinking or loop.index0 > qns.last_user %}
                {{- '<think>\n' ~ reasoning ~ '\n</think>\n\n' }}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endif %}
        {{- content }}

        {#- OpenAI-style tool calls -#}
        {%- set cn = namespace(count=0) %}
        {%- if 'tool_calls' in message and message['tool_calls'] and message['tool_calls'] is iterable and message['tool_calls'] is not mapping and message['tool_calls'] is not string %}
            {%- for raw_call in message['tool_calls'] %}
                {%- set call = raw_call %}
                {%- if raw_call is mapping and 'function' in raw_call and raw_call['function'] is mapping %}
                    {%- set call = raw_call['function'] %}
                {%- endif %}
                {%- set cname = 'unknown_function' %}
                {%- if call is mapping and 'name' in call and call['name'] is string %}
                    {%- set cname = call['name'] %}
                {%- endif %}
                {%- set cargs = '' %}
                {%- if call is mapping and 'arguments' in call %}
                    {%- set cargs = call['arguments'] %}
                {%- elif call is mapping and 'input' in call %}
                    {%- set cargs = call['input'] %}
                {%- endif %}
                {%- if cn.count == 0 %}
                    {%- if content %}
                        {{- '\n\n' }}
                    {%- endif %}
                {%- else %}
                    {{- '\n' }}
                {%- endif %}
                {{- emit_tool_call(tc_format, cname, cargs) }}
                {%- set cn.count = cn.count + 1 %}
            {%- endfor %}
        {%- endif %}

        {#- Anthropic-style tool_use blocks carried inside content -#}
        {%- set mc = message['content'] %}
        {%- if mc is iterable and mc is not string and mc is not mapping %}
            {%- for item in mc %}
                {%- if item is mapping and 'type' in item and item['type'] == 'tool_use' %}
                    {%- set cname = 'unknown_function' %}
                    {%- if 'name' in item and item['name'] is string %}
                        {%- set cname = item['name'] %}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {%- set cargs = '' %}
                    {%- if 'input' in item %}
                        {%- set cargs = item['input'] %}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {%- if cn.count == 0 %}
                        {%- if content %}
                            {{- '\n\n' }}
                        {%- endif %}
                    {%- else %}
                        {{- '\n' }}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {{- emit_tool_call(tc_format, cname, cargs) }}
                    {%- set cn.count = cn.count + 1 %}
                {%- endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
        {%- endif %}

        {{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}

    {%- else %}
        {#- user, and any unrecognized role, rendered as a user turn -#}
        {%- set tool_results = render_tool_results(message['content']) %}
        {%- set plain = render_content(message['content'], true) | trim %}

        {%- if tool_results | trim %}
            {%- if not st.tool_group_open %}
                {{- '<|im_start|>user' }}
                {%- set st.tool_group_open = true %}
            {%- endif %}
            {{- tool_results }}
            {%- if plain %}
                {{- '\n' ~ plain }}
                {{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}
                {%- set st.tool_group_open = false %}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- else %}
            {%- if st.tool_group_open %}
                {{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}
                {%- set st.tool_group_open = false %}
            {%- endif %}
            {{- '<|im_start|>user\n' ~ plain ~ '<|im_end|>\n' }}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if st.tool_group_open %}
    {{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}
    {%- set st.tool_group_open = false %}
{%- endif %}

{#- =====================================================================
    7. GENERATION PROMPT
===================================================================== -#}

{%- if add_generation_prompt %}
    {{- '<|im_start|>assistant\n' }}
    {%- if not think_on %}
        {#- Closed empty block suppresses reasoning. When thinking is on we
            emit nothing, so the model opens <think> itself and the reasoning
            parser sees a matched pair. -#}
        {{- '<think>\n\n</think>\n\n' }}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
